  "description": "50 liquid US large caps spanning all 11 GICS sectors. The competition universe for Season 2 onward.",
  "rationale": "Not the full S&P 500, and the reason is not rate limits: the vendor's grouped-daily endpoint returns the whole US market in one call, so 500 symbols cost exactly what 50 cost. The reasons are (1) 'S&P 500' means the constituents on a given date, and without point-in-time membership data a fixed list would bake in survivorship bias; (2) a 50-name snapshot can still be checked by hand against another source, which matters most in the first weeks of real data; (3) 11 sectors is what re-enables Autopsy's sector_rotation, which was disabled while the universe was two symbols. Widening to 500 is a change to this file, not to any code.",
